schema_version: 2
catalogs:
  - provider: claude
    backend: cli
    selection_mode: full
    source_cli: Claude
    cli_version: 2.1.282
    last_updated: 2026-09-25
    notes:
      - Model list and every model's effort line re-read 2026-09-25 by an agent-operated capture of
        the Claude Code 2.1.282 `/model` picker (Windows UI Automation visible text, checked
        against screenshots). Scope is the operator's subscription account; entitlement elsewhere
        is unverified. The operator's earlier four-row projection, collapsing the duplicate
        Default/Opus presentation to Opus, still applies.
      - "Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/claude-2.1.282/model-picker.agent-capture.redacted.txt"
      - The five source rows are Default (recommended), Opus (1M context), Fable, Sonnet, and Haiku.
        Default is a provider-default sentinel, not an executable model id. Its row and effort
        branch remain in evidence; Cats exposes only the four explicit model aliases, with Opus
        selected by default as the operator requested. This does not claim a provider-default alias
        will always resolve to Opus.
      - "Display names follow the operator's version-bearing projection of the picker descriptions:
        Opus 5.5 with 1M context, Fable 5.1, Sonnet 5, and Haiku 4.5. Cats adds the status suffix `
        (default)` in lowercase across model and effort menus; it is not part of the model name."
      - "Raw alias mappings: Opus executes `opus[1m]`, the token the picker's Opus (1M context) row
        saves. `sonnet` and `haiku` retain their 2.1.246 static-extraction provenance; `fable` and
        `claude-fable-5-1` retain the 2.1.258 help/static-artifact evidence. The existing Claude
        normalizers map these labels and all six effort values."
      - "Context aliases observed 2026-09-25 through `/status` on Claude Code 2.1.282 (interactive
        mode, operator's Max account): `opus` -> claude-opus-5-5 and `opus[1m]` ->
        claude-opus-5-5[1m]; `sonnet` -> claude-sonnet-5 and `sonnet[1m]` -> claude-sonnet-5[1m];
        `fable` and `fable[1m]` -> claude-fable-5-1. Plain aliases therefore run the standard
        context, and Fable drops the suffix. Print mode and other accounts were not probed.
        Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/claude-2.1.282/model-alias-status.redacted.txt"
      - "For Default, Opus, Fable, and Sonnet separately, the capture cycled the effort line with
        the Right key through Low, Medium, High, xHigh, Max, and Ultracode before it wrapped. Default
        and Opus mark Medium `(default)`; Fable and Sonnet mark High `(default)`. The starting xHigh
        line reflected the saved session effort, not a default. Haiku displays `Effort not supported
        for Haiku` and keeps `controls: []`. The Max usage warning is retained per model."
      - Older effort descriptions remain with their earlier provenance; they were not re-observed in
        2.1.282. In particular, the 2.1.258 static artifact maps Ultracode to `ultracode` and
        describes xHigh effort plus dynamic workflow orchestration; the earlier read-only `claude
        --effort ultracode --version` parser check accepted that token. This refresh does not repeat
        execution probes.
      - Opus 1M context was re-observed and now matches its `opus[1m]` execution. The Sonnet 1M
        value from the 2.1.246 static extraction is removed because `sonnet` resolves to the
        standard context; that standard value was not observed, so no limit is recorded. Haiku
        200K remains unverified 2.1.246 provenance; Fable context remains unknown and omitted.
    models:
      - default: true
        id: opus
        label: Opus 5.5 with 1M context
        capabilityTags:
          - tool_use
          - reasoning
        limits:
          contextWindowTokens: 1000000
        notes:
          - "Picker description: Opus 5.5 with 1M context - best for everyday, complex tasks"
          - The 2.1.282 picker marks Medium `(default)` for Opus; 2.1.273 marked High.
          - Executes `opus[1m]` (claude-opus-5-5[1m]); plain `opus` resolves to the standard-context
            claude-opus-5-5.
        source_names:
          - Opus
          - Opus 5 with 1M context
          - Opus 5.5 with 1M context
        execution:
          model: opus[1m]
        controls:
          - key: claude.reasoning_effort
            label: Reasoning effort
            description: Controls Claude Code effort for supported models.
            kind: enum
            scope: both
            values:
              - value: low
                label: Low
                description: Quick, straightforward implementation with minimal overhead
              - value: medium
                label: Medium
                description: Balanced approach with standard implementation and testing
              - value: high
                label: High
                description: Comprehensive implementation with extensive testing and documentation
              - value: xhigh
                label: xHigh
                description: Deeper reasoning than high, just below maximum (Fable 5, Opus 4.7+, Sonnet 5)
              - value: max
                label: Max
                description: Maximum capability with deepest reasoning. May use excessive tokens resulting in long
                  response times or overthinking. Use sparingly for the hardest tasks.
              - value: ultracode
                label: Ultracode
                description: "2.1.258 static artifact description: xHigh effort plus dynamic workflow orchestration
                  for this session only"
            semanticTags:
              - reasoning_intensity
            default: medium
      - default: false
        id: fable
        label: Fable 5.1
        capabilityTags:
          - tool_use
          - reasoning
        notes:
          - "Picker description: Fable 5.1 - most capable for your hardest and longest-running tasks"
        source_names:
          - Fable
          - Fable 5.1
        execution:
          model: fable
        controls:
          - key: claude.reasoning_effort
            label: Reasoning effort
            description: Controls Claude Code effort for supported models.
            kind: enum
            scope: both
            values:
              - value: low
                label: Low
                description: Quick, straightforward implementation with minimal overhead
              - value: medium
                label: Medium
                description: Balanced approach with standard implementation and testing
              - value: high
                label: High
                description: Comprehensive implementation with extensive testing and documentation
              - value: xhigh
                label: xHigh
                description: Deeper reasoning than high, just below maximum (Fable 5, Opus 4.7+, Sonnet 5)
              - value: max
                label: Max
                description: May use excessive tokens resulting in long response times or overthinking. Use
                  sparingly for the hardest tasks.
              - value: ultracode
                label: Ultracode
                description: "2.1.258 static artifact description: xHigh effort plus dynamic workflow orchestration
                  for this session only"
            semanticTags:
              - reasoning_intensity
            default: high
      - default: false
        id: sonnet
        label: Sonnet 5
        capabilityTags:
          - tool_use
        notes:
          - "Picker description: Sonnet 5 - efficient for routine tasks"
          - "`sonnet` resolves to the standard-context claude-sonnet-5; the 1M `sonnet[1m]` alias is
            not offered by the picker and is not used here."
        source_names:
          - Sonnet
          - Sonnet 5
        execution:
          model: sonnet
        controls:
          - key: claude.reasoning_effort
            label: Reasoning effort
            description: Controls Claude Code effort for supported models.
            kind: enum
            scope: both
            values:
              - value: low
                label: Low
                description: Quick, straightforward implementation with minimal overhead
              - value: medium
                label: Medium
                description: Balanced approach with standard implementation and testing
              - value: high
                label: High
                description: Comprehensive implementation with extensive testing and documentation
              - value: xhigh
                label: xHigh
                description: Deeper reasoning than high, just below maximum (Fable 5, Opus 4.7+, Sonnet 5)
              - value: max
                label: Max
                description: May use excessive tokens resulting in long response times or overthinking. Use
                  sparingly for the hardest tasks.
              - value: ultracode
                label: Ultracode
                description: "2.1.258 static artifact description: xHigh effort plus dynamic workflow orchestration
                  for this session only"
            semanticTags:
              - reasoning_intensity
            default: high
      - default: false
        id: haiku
        label: Haiku 4.5
        capabilityTags:
          - tool_use
          - latency_optimized
        limits:
          contextWindowTokens: 200000
        notes:
          - "Picker description: Haiku 4.5 - fastest for quick answers"
        source_names:
          - Haiku
          - Haiku 4.5
        execution:
          model: haiku
        controls: []
  - provider: codex
    backend: cli
    selection_mode: full
    source_cli: Codex
    cli_version: 0.156.1
    last_updated: 2026-09-24
    notes:
      - Complete visible model list and every per-model reasoning/advanced menu captured on 2026-09-24
        from Codex CLI 0.156.1 in Windows Terminal using UI Automation text and window screenshots.
        Scope is the local CLI account; entitlement on other accounts is unverified.
      - "Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/codex-0.156.1/picker.redacted.txt and
        docs/research/fixtures/codex-0.156.1/machine-catalog.redacted.json"
      - The seven picker rows agree with the seven visibility=list entries from codex debug models.
        The hidden gpt-reserve and codex-auto-review entries are enumeration evidence, not Cats picker
        rows. No existing picker row was removed.
      - Display labels preserve the exact GPT-style casing now observed in the picker. Raw slugs
        remain execution.model. Astra is explicitly (default); (current) masks that marker when Astra
        is active, so a per-invocation --model override to GPT-6-Sol exposed the default without
        changing config.toml.
      - Each model reasoning set/default was observed independently. Astra, GPT-6-Sol, GPT-5.6-Sol and
        GPT-5.6-Terra offer Max/Ultra; both Luna models offer Max only; GPT-5.5 ends at Extra high.
        GPT-5.6-Sol defaults to Low, all others to Medium.
      - The operator previously approved flattening More reasoning into one Cats effort list.
        Navigation, per-model usage warnings and advanced descriptions remain in the picker fixture.
        Max/Ultra display descriptions use the visible picker wording rather than the different
        machine enumeration descriptions.
      - Raw effort tokens/defaults and all seven 272000 context values were re-observed in codex debug
        models; these are CLI catalog values, not claims about OpenAI API limits. Older capability
        tags and migration source_names remain with their earlier provenance; no capability tags were
        inferred for new models.
    models:
      - default: true
        id: gpt-6-astra
        label: GPT-6-Astra
        capabilityTags:
          - tool_use
        notes:
          - Frontier intelligence for the most demanding work.
        source_names:
          - gpt-6-astra
        execution:
          model: gpt-6-astra
        controls:
          - key: codex.reasoning_effort
            label: Reasoning effort
            description: Controls Codex CLI reasoning depth for supported models.
            kind: enum
            scope: both
            values:
              - value: low
                label: Low
                description: Fast responses with lighter reasoning
              - value: medium
                label: Medium
                description: Balances speed and reasoning depth for everyday tasks
              - value: high
                label: High
                description: Greater reasoning depth for complex problems
              - value: xhigh
                label: Extra high
                description: Extra high reasoning depth for complex problems
              - value: max
                label: Max
                description: For difficult problems when quality matters more than speed · higher usage
              - value: ultra
                label: Ultra
                description: For demanding work using multiple agents · highest usage
            semanticTags:
              - reasoning_intensity
            default: medium
        limits:
          contextWindowTokens: 272000
      - default: false
        id: gpt-6-sol
        label: GPT-6-Sol
        limits:
          contextWindowTokens: 272000
        notes:
          - Workhorse model for coding and everyday work.
        execution:
          model: gpt-6-sol
        controls:
          - key: codex.reasoning_effort
            label: Reasoning effort
            description: Controls Codex CLI reasoning depth for supported models.
            kind: enum
            scope: both
            values:
              - value: low
                label: Low
                description: Fast responses with lighter reasoning
              - value: medium
                label: Medium
                description: Balances speed and reasoning depth for everyday tasks
              - value: high
                label: High
                description: Greater reasoning depth for complex problems
              - value: xhigh
                label: Extra high
                description: Extra high reasoning depth for complex problems
              - value: max
                label: Max
                description: For difficult problems when quality matters more than speed · higher usage
              - value: ultra
                label: Ultra
                description: For demanding work using multiple agents · highest usage
            semanticTags:
              - reasoning_intensity
            default: medium
      - default: false
        id: gpt-6-luna
        label: GPT-6-Luna
