  - provider: muse
    backend: cli
    selection_mode: full
    source_cli: Muse
    cli_version: 1.0.3-R2198.1
    last_updated: 2026-09-05
    notes:
      - First curated Meta Muse entry, added with the provider itself on 2026-09-05.
      - Model list read 2026-09-05 from muse's own `model/list` reply over the MSP host it serves on
        stdio (`muse serve`), which is its only enumeration surface - the CLI has no `models`
        subcommand and `muse exec` cannot list. The reply carried providerId `meta`, profileId
        `tbh`, and source `providerCatalog`, so the list is account-resolved and complete for this
        account.
      - "Evidence: docs/research/2026-09-05-meta-muse-cli-probe.md"
      - "`name` is the raw id `muse --model` accepts (the reply's `modelId`); `label` is a rendering
        of the reply's `displayLabel`, which upstream sets equal to the id."
      - The `-contributor` rows are the same models on terms Meta describes as "Your content,
        including inter-session messages, may be used for product improvement." They are listed so
        an operator can choose one deliberately.
      - No entry is marked default even though `model/list` flags `muse-spark-1.3-contributor` as
        `isDefault`. Projecting that here would make every runtime turn opt into content sharing
        without the operator asking for it; with no `--model` argument muse still uses whatever the
        account prefers.
      - "`context: 1007997` and `max_output: 128000` are the reply's `contextLimit` and
        `outputLimit`, identical across all four rows. `cost` is null upstream and is therefore
        omitted rather than guessed."
      - "Effort menus corrected from the operator on 2026-09-18: both 1.3 rows have minimal, low,
        medium, high, xhigh, max; both 1.2 rows stop at xhigh. No effort default is declared.
        Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/muse-unknown-version/efforts-2026-09-18.redacted.txt."
      - The earlier exec --help list proves parser vocabulary, not per-model picker
        availability/defaults. Model-list version, freshness, labels, and limits retain their
        2026-09-05 provenance; this correction only re-observes effort menus.
    models:
      - id: muse-spark-1.3
        label: muse-spark-1.3
        limits:
